# ── An Odoo addon's access rules are SOURCE, not bulk data ───────────────
# `*.csv` above had silently excluded every ir.model.access.csv since the
# connector was written — not one had ever been committed. The modules worked
# only because the files existed on one developer's disk; a clean clone
# installed them with NO access rules, and an Odoo model without those is
# unusable by exactly the stock users the review queue is built for.
#
# It stayed invisible because every local run had the files and only a fresh
# checkout does not. test_declared_data_files_are_tracked_in_git now fails if
# any manifest lists a file git does not have.
!connectors/odoo/*/security/*.csv

# ── The shipped market matrix is SOURCE, not bulk data ───────────────────
# Same trap as the Odoo access rules above, one directory over: `*.csv` would
# have swallowed the national competitor matrix, and the release packager
# copies from the working tree — so it built fine here and every clean
# checkout, CI run and client zip would have shipped site selection with no
# competitive field at all. That failure is silent by construction: a site
# with no rivals scores as opportunity, not as missing data.
#
# ~12 KB, and it travels with its ODbL notice (geo_sources.load_pack refuses
# a pack without one). test_market_pack asserts both ship.
!oasis/data/market_packs/*.csv

# Client state, per install, never ours to commit: their own fetched extract,
# their chain profiles, and the corrections they have made to the field.
oasis/data/competitor_overrides.json
oasis/data/competitor_network.csv
competitor_network.csv
# Which region THIS install fetched competitors over. Per install, and written
