# ── 2026-08-01 hygiene: engine/test output that kept dirtying the tree ───
# All three were TRACKED, so the rules above could never take effect — an
# ignore rule does nothing to a file already in the index. Untracked with
# `git rm --cached`; they stay on disk and simply stop being committed.
# (mock_pos_erp_showcase.db needs no rule of its own — `*.db` above covers it
# the moment it is out of the index.)
oasis/data/mande_purge_report.json
test_shadow_report.docx

# ── 2026-08-14: RXL port leftovers that must never enter history ─────────
# SQL Server database dumps taken while porting onto RXL. The TESTING11 one
# alone is 86MB, and git keeps a blob forever once committed — a single
# `git add -A` would be unrecoverable without rewriting history.
*.bak
# The hub's live admin key. Same class as connectors/odoo/.hub_state.json
# above: a real credential that happens to live inside the tree.
oasis_hub/.oasis_hub_admin_key

# Derived depot seed — rebuild with connectors/odoo/build_store_network_seed.py
# then differentiate_store_network.py (source stores_network.json is tracked)
connectors/odoo/store_network_seed.json

# generated live snapshots of the depot
connectors/odoo/live_view.html
connectors/odoo/_live_view.json

# ── 2026-08-21: the blobs that made this repo unpushable ────────────────
# A 2.0GB architecture snapshot (committed in 0705d4ae) plus three copies of
# a 118MB showcase DB and a 296MB test DB. GitHub hard-rejects any file over
# 100MB, so every push failed until the history was rewritten to drop them.
# The 2026-08-14 warning above was exactly right and arrived too late.
# All of them still live on disk; none may re-enter the index.
oasis_vault/System_Backups/
